Ticket [#4471](https://github.com/RadoslawZuchowski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues) was closed on 5 October after an engineering update. The original export shows **two distinct causes** among 412 unique reports; its pages overlap, so repeated report IDs are counted once. The desk's update changes what happens next: the parser issue is fixed, and the booking-v3 hint issue will not be fixed because that form was retired.

## The problems

### Day-first dates parsed month-first · 379 reports

The shared parser read month first. For tenants whose locale writes the day before the month, this could swap the day and month, causing bookings and reminders to land on the wrong day. These 379 reports cover all 11 tenants and span 1 April to 4 October 2026. **Status: fixed.** Engineering recorded `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.

Track this cause in [issue #1](https://github.com/RadoslawZuchowski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

### booking-v3 hint conflicts with day-first tenant dates · 33 reports

Three day-first tenants used booking-v3, whose field hint said `MM/DD/YYYY`. People followed that hint, but the form interpreted their entry in the tenant's day-first order. This was separate from the shared parser bug. The 33 reports span 17 April to 22 September 2026. **Status: won't fix.** The form was retired.

Track this cause in [issue #2](https://github.com/RadoslawZuchowski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Recount the ticket

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The intake tag is only a guess; classify each report using its tenant locale, booking form, and channel. Keep the causes in separate tickets: one records the completed parser fix, while the other records the retired form and the decision not to fix it.

